%I A400437 #11 Oct 08 2026 16:18:49
%S A400437 1,4,4,6,6,8,8,8,9,12,12,12,14,12,15,14,18,17,20,18,18,18,24,20,20
%N A400437 Maximum number of points that can be chosen from the n X n discrete torus Z_n X Z_n so that no three of them lie on a line.
%C A400437 A line of Z_n X Z_n is a set {(a + w*t1, b + w*t2): w in Z_n} with gcd(t1, t2, n) = 1, i.e., a coset of a cyclic subgroup of order n. Equivalently, three points lie on a line if they have lifts to Z X Z that are collinear.
%C A400437 a(n) <= 2n (Misiak et al.), and a(p) = p + 1 for odd primes p.
%C A400437 Terms for n <= 21 and a(25) are from Kurz; a(22) and a(24) are from Stępień and Szymaszkiewicz. a(12)-a(19) were confirmed independently by SAT search (see linked file).
%C A400437 Known lower bounds for the next terms: a(26) >= 20, a(27) >= 20, a(28) >= 24, a(30) >= 24, a(32) >= 23, a(33) >= 24, a(34) >= 24, a(35) >= 27, a(36) >= 27, a(38) >= 26, a(39) >= 26, a(40) >= 27. The bounds for n = 28, 30, 33, 34, 35, 36, 38, 39, 40 improve those of Stępień and Szymaszkiewicz; the corresponding point sets are in the linked file.
%H A400437 Jim Fowler, Andrew Groot, Deven Pandya and Bart Snapp, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.6604">The no-three-in-line problem on a torus</a>, arXiv:1203.6604 [math.CO], 2012.
%H A400437 Cheng Yeaw Ku and Kok Bin Wong, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00373-018-1878-8">On no-three-in-line problem on m-dimensional torus</a>, Graphs and Combinatorics 34 (2018), 355-364.
%H A400437 Sascha Kurz, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.4333">Caps in Z_n^2</a>, Serdica J. Computing 3 (2009), 159-178; arXiv:1401.4333 [math.CO], 2014.
%H A400437 Aleksander Misiak, Zofia Stępień, Alicja Szymaszkiewicz, Lucjan Szymaszkiewicz and Maciej Zwierzchowski, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2015.08.006">A note on the no-three-in-line problem on a torus</a>, Discrete Math. 339 (2016), 217-221; arXiv:1406.6713 [math.CO].
%H A400437 Azmi C. Özgen, <a href="/A400437/a400437.txt">Witnesses, SAT confirmation of a(12)-a(19), improved lower bounds for n <= 40, and a checker</a>
%H A400437 Azmi C. Özgen, <a href="/A400437/a400437.py.txt">Python program</a>
%H A400437 Zofia Stępień, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s00026-020-00503-6">Ovals in Z^2_{2p}</a>, Ann. Comb. 24 (2020), 549-555.
%H A400437 Zofia Stępień and Lucjan Szymaszkiewicz, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10878-017-0171-8">Arcs in Z^2_{2p}</a>, J. Comb. Optim. 35 (2018), 341-349; arXiv:1512.02175 [math.CO].
%e A400437 a(3) = 4: for example {(0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1)}. Z_3 X Z_3 is the affine plane of order 3, in which no 5 points are free of collinear triples.
